**How to implement.** The absorbing triclinic builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'AbsorbingTriclinicParameters gets AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildAbsorbing`'s (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:buildAbsorbing`) with `p` read as `this`: ε is the complex symmetric matrix with diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²) + i(ε″₁₁, ε″₂₂, ε″₃₃) and off-diagonal i·ε″₁₂, i·ε″₁₃, i·ε″₂₃ through `Eps.create`, μ is `Mu.vacuum`, and ρ is the purely imaginary symmetric matrix of the six gyration components through `Rho.create`, the same entries in the same order. Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of an absorbing triclinic gyrotropic crystal; ε″ is general in the ε′ frame and ρ stays imaginary (spec 0050 §3.16; specs/0044/.manual/018-absorbing-biaxial-inverse.md). (2) Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs MUST retain buildAbsorbing with its concrete parameter and return signature; its body MUST become a call to p.opticalProperties. Only the tensor-construction expression moves to the product member; the ground-truth/design builder itself MUST remain in this module and move with it to BerremanTestSupport in step 346, as 001 §Q requires. The old tensor body MUST be deleted in this step, leaving one implementation of the arithmetic. Its short contract comment MUST describe the builder without claiming a product destination. (3) AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests MUST continue calling buildAbsorbing for their forward models and direct tensor assertions; no test is deleted, no expected value or tolerance changes, and no product project references test support.  BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member builds the same complex entries by the same operations. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, 7 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member; `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s) is not selected.

**Acceptance.** After extracting shared tensor construction, AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties MUST hold the single kernel and AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing MUST remain a test-side caller of that kernel, preserving every forward-model result and its required move to BerremanTestSupport; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
